% Refinement-sort machinery (TODO_0011 rung 1) — membership as PROVABLE facts.
%
% Sorts are EXTRINSIC refinements (Lovas–Pfenning): one content-addressed
% term may inhabit many sorts; membership is a judgment, erased at runtime.
% A subsort declaration `A <: B.` is sugar for a persistent sedge fact
% (synthesized by the loader); the order the checker enforces is the
% reflexive-transitive closure below. The engine's sort DAG
% (lib/engine/sorts.js) is a compiled INDEX over exactly these clauses —
% the table is optimization, membership proof is semantics.
%
% Importing this file is the opt-in: a calculus without it has no sort
% machinery (absent, not disabled). Programs contribute the facts:
% `bin <: q.` beside the numeric prelude, `wood: resource.` classifiers
% in game files. ILL stays sortless.

sort: type.                             % the classifier of sort names

sedge: (a: sort) -> (b: sort) -> type.  % declared subsort edge
leq:   (a: sort) -> (b: sort) -> type.  % subsort order (closure)

leq/refl: leq S S.
leq/step: leq S U
  <- sedge S T
  <- leq T U.
